WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:03.150
‘You all know exactly who I am.’

00:00:03.150 --> 00:00:07.339
The bald chemistry teacher looked around at
the men surrounding him in the desert.

00:00:07.339 --> 00:00:10.590
Cadillacs, leather jackets, blacked-out shades.

00:00:10.590 --> 00:00:15.889
The gang members shifted nervously from foot
to foot as the man bragged openly about what

00:00:15.889 --> 00:00:18.900
he’s done to build his criminal empire.

00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:23.439
Walter White’s attention turned back to
the man in front of him, a slight sneer played

00:00:23.439 --> 00:00:25.160
around his lips.

00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:27.369
‘Now, say my name.’

00:00:27.369 --> 00:00:31.170
The man took a moment to reply as the desert
wind blew behind him.

00:00:31.170 --> 00:00:35.989
He seemed to be weighing his options, realizing
quickly that he had lost all control over

00:00:35.989 --> 00:00:37.210
the situation.

00:00:37.210 --> 00:00:38.210
‘Heisenberg.’

00:00:38.210 --> 00:00:39.910
‘You’re g-’

00:00:39.910 --> 00:00:40.910
BANG!

00:00:40.910 --> 00:00:42.989
Walter White fell to the ground dead.

00:00:42.989 --> 00:00:47.600
The characters all around yelped in surprise,
drew their guns, and started wildly pointing

00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:52.380
them around the circle, trying to figure out
who killed the great Heisenberg.

00:00:52.380 --> 00:00:56.600
But his killer just stared in awe from his
couch in the front room as the Netflix show

00:00:56.600 --> 00:00:58.670
kept playing on the TV.

00:00:58.670 --> 00:01:02.090
Had the toy gun in his hand really done that?

00:01:02.090 --> 00:01:03.090
*

00:01:03.090 --> 00:01:06.240
Josh had admitted to himself that he had a
problem a long time ago.

00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:12.140
But at least being a yard-sale addict was
cheaper than just a regular old retail addict.

00:01:12.140 --> 00:01:16.700
Actually in truth, he was also an estate-sale
addict, a garage-sale addict and a thrift

00:01:16.700 --> 00:01:18.110
store addict.

00:01:18.110 --> 00:01:23.240
Anywhere you could buy people’s old junk
for rock-bottom prices, he’d sniff it out.

00:01:23.240 --> 00:01:27.939
The Saturday that his life changed forever
was just like any other Saturday, really.

00:01:27.939 --> 00:01:33.290
In the sweaty heat of the Atlantic City suburbs,
he hadn’t meant to stop by any sales today,

00:01:33.290 --> 00:01:36.000
but one just so happened to catch his eye.

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:41.090
There was a box marked ‘Nerd Stuff’ and
he took that as a personal challenge.

00:01:41.090 --> 00:01:45.479
Was this some old lady’s version of nerd
stuff or a veteran Dungeon Master’s treasure

00:01:45.479 --> 00:01:46.479
trove?

00:01:46.479 --> 00:01:48.840
The reality was somewhere in-between the two.

00:01:48.840 --> 00:01:54.030
There were a couple of seasons of Buffy on
VHS, a copy of the original Deus Ex, and some

00:01:54.030 --> 00:01:55.940
Legend of Zelda plushies.

00:01:55.940 --> 00:02:00.390
It hadn’t really been worth stopping his
car for, except for a little plastic splash

00:02:00.390 --> 00:02:02.590
of color that caught his eye.

00:02:02.590 --> 00:02:06.950
Josh reached way down to the bottom of the
box and rooted around for it.

00:02:06.950 --> 00:02:11.340
There was no way, it couldn’t possibly be
the toy he’d spent all his childhood asking

00:02:11.340 --> 00:02:12.720
for and never getting.

00:02:12.720 --> 00:02:14.650
But it was!

00:02:14.650 --> 00:02:18.620
A 1985 Nintendo Entertainment System Zapper!

00:02:18.620 --> 00:02:24.530
With an orange grip and barrel, NES gray bodywork,
and the beautiful font printed along the side,

00:02:24.530 --> 00:02:26.450
it was unmistakable.

00:02:26.450 --> 00:02:31.360
He threw a wad of cash at the old lady behind
the table and rushed back into his car, quickly

00:02:31.360 --> 00:02:32.450
as he could.

00:02:32.450 --> 00:02:37.540
It was time to cancel his day plans, he had
a childhood dream to fulfill!

00:02:37.540 --> 00:02:43.000
But no sooner than he had got home and flipped
on his TV, the dream came crashing down around

00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:44.000
him.

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:48.940
His old NES, the one he’d had since he was
a little kid, had sadly keeled over.

00:02:48.940 --> 00:02:52.239
It refused to power on, no matter what he
did.

00:02:52.239 --> 00:02:55.170
So that made his Zapper pretty much useless.

00:02:55.170 --> 00:03:00.390
The best he could do with it now would be
to point it at the TV and make pew pew noises

00:03:00.390 --> 00:03:01.670
with his mouth.

00:03:01.670 --> 00:03:06.080
So Josh opened up Netflix and put on an episode
of Breaking Bad.

00:03:06.080 --> 00:03:11.489
Little did he know, as he raised the Zapper
to the screen, that he was actually in possession

00:03:11.489 --> 00:03:14.210
of SCP-674.

00:03:14.210 --> 00:03:18.760
Nobody would know looking at it on the surface,
even the most hardcore gamers wouldn’t have

00:03:18.760 --> 00:03:23.030
a clue, because you can fully disassemble,
clean, and reassemble the Zapper and get no

00:03:23.030 --> 00:03:26.819
indication that it’s anything other than
what it appears to be.

00:03:26.819 --> 00:03:31.590
However, as soon as the gun is pointed at
a television screen or a computer monitor

00:03:31.590 --> 00:03:35.720
of any kind, it starts to pose a very real
threat.

00:03:35.720 --> 00:03:39.060
Or, at least, a very real fictional threat.

00:03:39.060 --> 00:03:43.620
If you shoot at the screen, whatever media
is playing on it at the time will react and

00:03:43.620 --> 00:03:46.340
adapt to what has just happened.

00:03:46.340 --> 00:03:49.879
That means characters on the screens will
react in accordance with the rules of their

00:03:49.879 --> 00:03:51.819
respective universes.

00:03:51.819 --> 00:03:56.730
In a grounded, realistic drama, the gunshot
will behave like any other, killing or wounding

00:03:56.730 --> 00:04:01.620
the victim with perhaps enough time for them
to give a dying monologue, but in an episode

00:04:01.620 --> 00:04:07.250
of Rick and Morty, the shot could manifest
in any number of bizarre creative ways.

00:04:07.250 --> 00:04:11.130
News crews that witness the user shooting
a person in their live report will continue

00:04:11.130 --> 00:04:14.989
to cover the incident as if it is part of
the ongoing story.

00:04:14.989 --> 00:04:19.169
If you shoot Walter White, he falls to the
ground dead.

00:04:19.169 --> 00:04:21.250
Josh stared at the screen in utter amazement.

00:04:21.250 --> 00:04:25.210
He didn’t expect the writers to kill off
their main character just like that.

00:04:25.210 --> 00:04:27.910
Wasn’t there supposed to be another 9 episodes?

00:04:27.910 --> 00:04:30.140
What would they do to fill all that time?

00:04:30.140 --> 00:04:34.699
As the episode played out, it seemed to mostly
just follow Jesse, trying desperately to escape

00:04:34.699 --> 00:04:36.720
with his money before it was too late.

00:04:36.720 --> 00:04:41.780
He kept glancing towards the camera for some
reason, with a slight look of fear in his

00:04:41.780 --> 00:04:42.780
eyes.

00:04:42.780 --> 00:04:44.670
Very strange creative decision there.

00:04:44.670 --> 00:04:48.380
Josh backed out of the show to scroll through
his “continue watching.”

00:04:48.380 --> 00:04:52.360
There was something a little creepy about
how he’d pointed that Zapper at the TV,

00:04:52.360 --> 00:04:57.350
pulled the trigger, and perfectly, at that
moment, a character had been shot.

00:04:57.350 --> 00:05:01.630
Time to pick out a show without any guns and
murder for a bit.

00:05:01.630 --> 00:05:02.640
Something safe.

00:05:02.640 --> 00:05:07.000
The familiar melodica tune filled the lounge
as various shots of Dunder Mifflin employees

00:05:07.000 --> 00:05:10.980
busied themselves, shredding credit cards
and answering phone calls.

00:05:10.980 --> 00:05:15.660
It never ceased to make his worries go away
seeing the words ‘The Office’ appear on

00:05:15.660 --> 00:05:16.750
the screen.

00:05:16.750 --> 00:05:20.540
He settled into the couch, watching as the
characters all gathered in the conference

00:05:20.540 --> 00:05:22.640
room for some first-aid training.

00:05:22.640 --> 00:05:27.130
The CPR dummy lay on the floor with Michael
Scott earnestly explaining to the woman that

00:05:27.130 --> 00:05:29.669
the victim appeared to have lost their limbs.

00:05:29.669 --> 00:05:34.510
He laughed along as the scene descended into
chaos, as none of the employees took the training

00:05:34.510 --> 00:05:36.150
seriously at all.

00:05:36.150 --> 00:05:40.169
Even though he’d seen this episode countless
times, it never got old.

00:05:40.169 --> 00:05:44.460
Absent-mindedly, he pointed the gun at the
TV and pulled the trigger.

00:05:44.460 --> 00:05:45.460
BANG!

00:05:45.460 --> 00:05:46.949
Pam collapsed on the ground.

00:05:46.949 --> 00:05:52.009
All of the characters dived out of the way,
trying to find cover behind their chairs,

00:05:52.009 --> 00:05:54.580
not daring to peek out at the camera.

00:05:54.580 --> 00:05:58.830
Only the first aid lady stayed on the scene,
trying her best to resuscitate Pam.

00:05:58.830 --> 00:06:02.080
It cut to a shot of Dwight talking to the
camera sadly.

00:06:02.080 --> 00:06:06.440
He said something that was almost funny, but
there was a real heaviness in the moment.

00:06:06.440 --> 00:06:10.069
His eyes were red, like he’d been crying
off-camera.

00:06:10.069 --> 00:06:14.139
Josh flipped the TV off and stared at himself
in the dark reflection.

00:06:14.139 --> 00:06:15.139
Was he dreaming?

00:06:15.139 --> 00:06:17.780
He hadn’t just done that… had he?

00:06:17.780 --> 00:06:23.560
Fortunately for Josh and for the rest of humanity,
he had not killed Jenna Fisher or Bryan Cranston.

00:06:23.560 --> 00:06:27.660
He hadn’t even killed their characters in
the shows, at least not for anyone other than

00:06:27.660 --> 00:06:29.010
himself.

00:06:29.010 --> 00:06:34.500
Research into SCP-674 shows that the appearance
of characters being killed off on screen only

00:06:34.500 --> 00:06:37.099
exists in the mind of the shooter.

00:06:37.099 --> 00:06:40.819
For everyone else, The Office remains the
same as it always was.

00:06:40.819 --> 00:06:45.319
Unfortunately for Josh, however, Pam is now
dead in that universe and will always be whenever

00:06:45.319 --> 00:06:46.979
he watches an episode.

00:06:46.979 --> 00:06:51.500
It leaves a real shadow over the later seasons,
but the characters apparently manage to do

00:06:51.500 --> 00:06:55.020
a good job pivoting into its new darker tone.

00:06:55.020 --> 00:06:59.800
Other shows that have been tested in research
conditions have yielded interesting results.

00:06:59.800 --> 00:07:04.220
Like in Star Trek, it is impossible to actually
kill Captain Kirk.

00:07:04.220 --> 00:07:08.300
Instead, various red shirts always just so
happen to dive in front of him or fall into

00:07:08.300 --> 00:07:10.410
frame at the pivotal moment.

00:07:10.410 --> 00:07:14.270
With a small dead zone on the right-hand side
of the screen, characters who witness enough

00:07:14.270 --> 00:07:18.730
shootings have the sense to stick to that
side of the frame whenever the shot is on

00:07:18.730 --> 00:07:23.770
them, sometimes going so far as to plead directly
with the viewer, breaking the fourth wall

00:07:23.770 --> 00:07:26.009
in their desperation to survive.

00:07:26.009 --> 00:07:30.860
When Josh came back from a long walk outside,
he’d convinced himself that what he had

00:07:30.860 --> 00:07:33.849
seen earlier was all just some vivid dream.

00:07:33.849 --> 00:07:39.020
A dream he didn’t remember waking up from
but definitely wasn’t happening anymore.

00:07:39.020 --> 00:07:41.860
He’d play some video games, that’s what
he’d do.

00:07:41.860 --> 00:07:46.960
He had decided he would just play some Super
Smash Bros and unwind.

00:07:46.960 --> 00:07:50.850
Anyone who has ever said that sentence to
themselves will know firsthand how foolish

00:07:50.850 --> 00:07:52.090
that is.

00:07:52.090 --> 00:07:57.090
Not ten minutes later, Josh had definitely
forgotten all about his dream from before.

00:07:57.090 --> 00:08:00.090
He was too busy raging and cursing at the
screen.

00:08:00.090 --> 00:08:05.389
He couldn’t stand playing against King Dedede,
that stupid hammer move always got him.

00:08:05.389 --> 00:08:09.380
Without thinking, Josh snatched the Zapper
from the couch next to him and blasted Dedede

00:08:09.380 --> 00:08:10.879
right in the face.

00:08:10.879 --> 00:08:15.810
In classic Smash Bros style, the giant penguin
king was launched backwards, flying off the

00:08:15.810 --> 00:08:18.539
screen in a blast of colorful smoke.

00:08:18.539 --> 00:08:20.250
But he didn’t respawn.

00:08:20.250 --> 00:08:23.569
For a second, his character just stood on
the screen awkwardly before it kicked him

00:08:23.569 --> 00:08:26.199
back out to the character select screen.

00:08:26.199 --> 00:08:29.569
This time though, King Dedede’s picture
was missing.

00:08:29.569 --> 00:08:31.090
Josh couldn’t help himself.

00:08:31.090 --> 00:08:35.490
He set up a free for all match straight away,
picking all of the characters he hated to

00:08:35.490 --> 00:08:36.490
fight against.

00:08:36.490 --> 00:08:41.940
Sonic, Mario, Pikachu, Bowser, Link, Nes,
even Wii Fit Trainer.

00:08:41.940 --> 00:08:43.599
One after the other.

00:08:43.599 --> 00:08:45.560
Bang bang bang!

00:08:45.560 --> 00:08:49.339
He felt a strange sense of satisfaction once
he’d done his work.

00:08:49.339 --> 00:08:53.740
Great, now the character list only had the
fair, balanced ones left.

00:08:53.740 --> 00:08:57.030
They just so happened to all be his favorite
characters too.

00:08:57.030 --> 00:08:58.610
But why stop there?

00:08:58.610 --> 00:09:03.120
Josh jumped across to Elden Ring and marched
his knight up through the gate to Stormveil

00:09:03.120 --> 00:09:04.120
Castle.

00:09:04.120 --> 00:09:08.100
Before Margit had even gotten through his
opening cutscene, Josh had shot the boss right

00:09:08.100 --> 00:09:09.290
in the face.

00:09:09.290 --> 00:09:14.330
This boss battle that he’d been stuck on
for hours was over before it even started.

00:09:14.330 --> 00:09:15.589
What else could he do now?

00:09:15.589 --> 00:09:20.110
He put on an episode of Stranger Things and
shot the Demogorgon, then Moff Gideon in the

00:09:20.110 --> 00:09:23.350
Mandalorian, and some goblins in Hogwarts
Legacy.

00:09:23.350 --> 00:09:27.910
The clickers from the Last of Us took a couple
of extra shots but went down easy enough.

00:09:27.910 --> 00:09:32.540
He went over to his PC and killed the Ender
Dragon in Minecraft without blowing up any

00:09:32.540 --> 00:09:33.540
beds.

00:09:33.540 --> 00:09:37.970
He won a game of Rocket League 53-0 after
he shot both cars on the opposing team.

00:09:37.970 --> 00:09:41.339
He played through DOORS in Roblox without
a single jumpscare.

00:09:41.339 --> 00:09:45.160
He’d just shoot any monster that filled
his screen.

00:09:45.160 --> 00:09:46.279
What could be better?

00:09:46.279 --> 00:09:48.589
He reckoned it was time for more movies.

00:09:48.589 --> 00:09:53.269
Walking back across the lounge, spinning the
gun around his finger like a Western, he wondered

00:09:53.269 --> 00:09:58.260
if now would be a good chance to hunt down
all the legendary animals in Red Dead 2.

00:09:58.260 --> 00:10:03.380
It would certainly make the job a lot easier
if he could kill them all in just one shot.

00:10:03.380 --> 00:10:06.920
He’d just need to be careful not to shoot
Arthur by accident.

00:10:06.920 --> 00:10:08.860
But then Josh sat on the remote.

00:10:08.860 --> 00:10:13.880
The TV flicked over to an old rerun of Bob
Ross just as he’d been squaring up to shoot.

00:10:13.880 --> 00:10:16.430
He pulled the trigger before he could react.

00:10:16.430 --> 00:10:18.680
The canvas was spattered red.

00:10:18.680 --> 00:10:23.670
From somewhere off-camera he heard the artist’s
wheezing voice try to comfort him.

00:10:23.670 --> 00:10:28.459
‘There are no mistakes, just happy…’

00:10:28.459 --> 00:10:30.929
But he died before he could say another word.

00:10:30.929 --> 00:10:31.929
*

00:10:31.929 --> 00:10:35.090
The Exposition Gun first came onto the SCP
Foundation’s radar when a strange police

00:10:35.090 --> 00:10:39.519
report was doing the rounds on an email chain
amongst local authorities.

00:10:39.519 --> 00:10:44.430
They were all finding a great deal of value
from a man called Josh, who had turned himself

00:10:44.430 --> 00:10:49.389
in at his local station in Atlantic City for
‘killing like everyone’.

00:10:49.389 --> 00:10:54.830
Naturally, the police took his report very
seriously, for all of about 10 minutes.

00:10:54.830 --> 00:10:59.090
As soon as they realized that he was talking
about video games, TV, and movie characters,

00:10:59.090 --> 00:11:01.760
the whole case turned into one big joke.

00:11:01.760 --> 00:11:06.590
They sat Josh down in front of a TV and played
him episodes of the shows he was talking about,

00:11:06.590 --> 00:11:11.490
pointing out characters still alive in scenes
after he’d supposedly shot them to death,

00:11:11.490 --> 00:11:16.450
but he seemed to just grow more distressed
as he realized he was experiencing this phenomenon

00:11:16.450 --> 00:11:17.450
alone.

00:11:17.450 --> 00:11:22.100
By the time, Foundation agents tracked Josh
down and took him in for questioning, the

00:11:22.100 --> 00:11:23.339
gun had moved on.

00:11:23.339 --> 00:11:27.079
He’d marched it straight back to the old
lady who’d sold it to him, who had then

00:11:27.079 --> 00:11:28.630
sold it on again.

00:11:28.630 --> 00:11:33.640
Josh’s full account of events and description
of the Zapper were taken before he was administered

00:11:33.640 --> 00:11:39.370
Class C amnestics and allowed to continue
with his yard-sale addiction uninhibited.

00:11:39.370 --> 00:11:45.470
SCP-674 was found some time later in the possession
of a 33-year-old Caucasian male simply referred

00:11:45.470 --> 00:11:52.459
to as Mr S. A reclusive man in a neighboring
city, Mr S first gained the SCP Foundation's

00:11:52.459 --> 00:11:57.600
attention through his extremist political
blog, in which he claimed to have assassinated

00:11:57.600 --> 00:12:01.730
prominent political figures, news anchors,
and talk show hosts.

00:12:01.730 --> 00:12:06.970
While the truth of those claims was demonstrably
false, it was clear from the way he described

00:12:06.970 --> 00:12:10.380
events that he really did believe the delusion.

00:12:10.380 --> 00:12:13.800
After being questioned, it was discovered
that he had never left his home.

00:12:13.800 --> 00:12:18.610
Instead, he stayed on his couch, watching
news reports and firing at any prominent figures

00:12:18.610 --> 00:12:23.080
that appeared, believing that he was indeed
killing them in the real world.

00:12:23.080 --> 00:12:28.230
Despite claiming that he was using SCP-674
to prevent a military police state, using

00:12:28.230 --> 00:12:33.279
the device to "assassinate" so many high-profile
figures had the opposite effect on his video

00:12:33.279 --> 00:12:34.290
reality.

00:12:34.290 --> 00:12:40.380
In his blog posts, he described an increasingly
unstable global order, martial law, and catastrophic

00:12:40.380 --> 00:12:45.140
events consistent with the hypothetical release
of two deadly SCPs.

00:12:45.140 --> 00:12:49.620
His house was barricaded, with security cameras
set up in every direction.

00:12:49.620 --> 00:12:54.990
The more he had been using the gun, the more
the characters and journalists on TV had threatened

00:12:54.990 --> 00:12:59.500
him, claiming that the SCP Foundation were
on their way to apprehend him and that he

00:12:59.500 --> 00:13:02.700
would face retribution for what he had been
doing.

00:13:02.700 --> 00:13:06.070
Mr S’s intended ambush of Foundation agents
failed.

00:13:06.070 --> 00:13:10.930
While they appeared to be dying on the security
feeds he had set up, the agents experienced

00:13:10.930 --> 00:13:17.649
no physical harm in reality as they apprehended
the man and seized SCP-674.

00:13:17.649 --> 00:13:22.870
While the majority of researchers have deemed
that SCP-674 is harmless to all but the mental

00:13:22.870 --> 00:13:28.769
well-being of the shooter, there was a notably
sinister result to Mr S’s time in Foundation

00:13:28.769 --> 00:13:29.889
detention.

00:13:29.889 --> 00:13:34.870
Alone in his cell, Mr S soon started to engage
in heated arguments with the security camera

00:13:34.870 --> 00:13:36.640
set up to monitor him.

00:13:36.640 --> 00:13:41.250
There is no record of any voices in the room
other than his own, yet he seemed to be locked

00:13:41.250 --> 00:13:43.100
in a fierce argument.

00:13:43.100 --> 00:13:48.300
All of a sudden, Mr S dropped to the ground
dead with three .38 caliber handgun bullets

00:13:48.300 --> 00:13:50.190
lodged in his chest.

00:13:50.190 --> 00:13:55.610
The entirety of his holding cell was searched
for evidence of a shooter, but none was found.

00:13:55.610 --> 00:14:00.509
The Exposition Gun remains in a locked plastic
case in Storage Site 23.

00:14:00.509 --> 00:14:04.700
Aside from regular cleaning and maintenance,
it is used under controlled circumstances

00:14:04.700 --> 00:14:08.959
to creatively gather intelligence about further
SCP activity.

00:14:08.959 --> 00:14:13.490
In the event of the site being compromised,
personnel are allowed to destroy the Exposition

00:14:13.490 --> 00:14:18.440
Gun at their own discretion, should it fall
into the wrong hands.

00:14:18.440 --> 00:14:23.470
Now check out “SCP-348 - A Gift from Dad”
and “SCP-978 - Desire Camera” for more!

